From: Tai Gar maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] Unlink JSContext from the GC list when class_proto allocation fails

JS_NewContextRaw() registers the new context with add_gc_object() before
allocating class_proto. When that allocation fails, the context is freed
while still linked in rt->gc_obj_list, and the JS_RunGC() inside a later
JS_FreeRuntime() reads the freed header (use-after-free).

Upstream quickjs-ng df836d1 and 19dbe85 both contain the defect.
Found by Tai's loader-thread allocation failure sweep.
---
--- a/quickjs.c
+++ b/quickjs.c
@@ -2863,6 +2863,7 @@
     ctx->class_proto = js_malloc_rt(rt, sizeof(ctx->class_proto[0]) *
                                     rt->class_count);
     if (!ctx->class_proto) {
+        remove_gc_object(&ctx->header);
         js_free_rt(rt, ctx);
         return NULL;
     }
